Invariant Preservation:
  - Row ordering MUST be preserved (SPARQL semantic requirement)
  - Column ordering fixed by query structure
  - Element values bit-exact (no tolerance needed)
  - Winner: IdTable::operator== (preserves all invariants)

Minimality:
  - IdTable::operator== already exists (0 new lines of code)
  - Digest approach requires ResultDigest integration (20+ lines)
  - Sort approach requires temporary tables + sort (30+ lines)
  - Winner: IdTable::operator== (minimal structure)

CONVERGENCE DECISION: Use existing IdTable::operator== (monoidal composition)

